notes = "(!) The ROMs go in system/oricutron/roms/, with the names Oricutron uses: basic11b.rom for the Atmos (the default machine), basic10.rom for the Oric-1, microdis.rom for disk images.|(!) Copy the .pch and .sym files from Oricutron's roms/ directory there too: the .pch files tell the core where the ROM's tape routines are, for fast tape loading.|(!) Tape images (.tap, .ort) are loaded with CLOAD, typed in for you; disk images (.dsk) boot the matching disk system.|(!) The RetroPad's d-pad is the cursor keys, A and B are Space, Start is Return, X is Esc and Y is Ctrl. The frontend's keyboard is the Oric's keyboard."

description = "A port of Oricutron, Peter Gordon's emulator of the Oric-1, Oric Atmos, Telestrat and Pravetz 8D, to libretro: tape and disk images (Microdisc, Jasmin, Byte Drive 500, Pravetz), the AY-3-8912 sound, keyboard and pads."
